No code of qpdf is in cera. Its sources libqpdf/QPDF_linearization.cc and
libqpdf/QPDFWriter.cc, and the chapter on linearization of its manual,
were read to learn how a linearised file is laid out so that readers
accept it: which part of the file an object belongs to by who refers to
it, which of two parts wins, in what order objects are walked and
numbered, where the two cross-reference sections go, and what the hint
tables say. qpdf's check of linearised files (qpdf --check-linearization)
is what cera's output is tested against.

What is in linear.go was written for cera, in Go and to its own design,
and is under cera's licence. This notice is the credit qpdf's authors are
due for the knowledge.
